# GLM 4.6 Flash — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: Z.ai / OpenCode Zen (`opencode/glm-4.6-flash`; text-only "Flash" free variant; **no AA page (404) / no OpenRouter page (404) / not in Z.ai's official lineup or the current OpenCode Zen catalog**)
- Date: 2026-11-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Verdict — SELF-EXCLUDED.** **GLM 4.6 Flash** is presented as **"Z.ai's free text-only Flash variant of GLM-4.6 (128K, tool calling, reasoning)"**, but it cannot be scored under the research-permanence and no-invented-numbers rules because **(a) it has no benchmark of its own** — the curated `meta` states verbatim **"no published Flash-specific benchmarks; Z.ai publishes flagship numbers only,"** and every source that mentions it either points at the **GLM-4.6 flagship's** numbers or publishes none; **(b) its identity as a distinct Z.ai text release is unconfirmed** — Z.ai's documented GLM-4.6 generation is the **355B/32B flagship (200K ctx)** plus the **GLM-4.6V / GLM-4.6V-Flash (9B) vision** line, and the free *text* "Flash" tiers Z.ai actually names are **GLM-4.5-Flash** and **GLM-4.7-Flash (30B-A3B)** — there is **no official "GLM-4.6-Flash" text card**; **(c) no independent tracker covers it** — **Artificial Analysis returns 404** (no Intelligence Index / Speed / Cost) and **OpenRouter returns 404** (not served as a distinct route); and **(d) it is not even in the current OpenCode Zen model table** (which lists `glm-4.6`, `glm-5.3-flash`, `glm-5.3-flash-free` — not `glm-4.6-flash`). Any capability vector here would be a re-badging of the flagship's or a sibling's measurements onto an unmapped, unmeasured name — so the entry is excluded, not scored.

## Why this is a self-exclusion (not a scored model)

- **No Flash-specific benchmark exists — the only data are the flagship's.** The curated record is explicit: **"no published Flash-specific benchmarks; Z.ai publishes flagship numbers only."** Z.ai's own **GLM-4.6 documentation** (fetched 2026-11-01) describes only the **flagship** — "expanded from 128K to **200K** tokens," **128K max output**, text in/out, evaluated on "8 authoritative benchmarks… AIME 25, GPQA, LCB v6, HLE, SWE-Bench Verified" — all under the **GLM-4.6** name, **not** a "Flash" checkpoint. Crediting those to GLM-4.6-Flash would be **reattribution**.
- **Not a documented Z.ai text release.** A third-party GLM lineup survey (**secondtalent.com, "Every GLM model explained," Sep 2026**) tabulates the whole family and lists the **free text Flashes as GLM-4.7-Flash (30B/3B) and GLM-4.5-Flash**, and the **9B GLM-4.6V-Flash** (a **vision** model). It shows **GLM-4.6 (Sep 30 2025, GLM-4.5 architecture, 200K)** as flagship with **no accompanying "GLM-4.6-Flash" text sibling** — the point releases (4.6/4.7) shipped on the flagship architecture; the small *text* "Flash/air" tiers belong to 4.5 and 4.7, not 4.6.
- **No independent measurement — AA and OpenRouter both 404.** **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/glm-4-6-flash` → 404** (no Intelligence Index, no Speed, no Cost, no verbosity). **`openrouter.ai/z-ai/glm-4.6-flash` → 404** (GLM-4.6 flagship *is* routed by 4 providers — DeepInfra/Venice/NovitaAI/Z.ai — but the "Flash" text variant is not a listed route). No LMArena, no Vals, no leaderboard cell tied to this name.
- **Absent from the current serving catalog.** OpenCode Zen's live model table (fetched 2026-11-01) lists **`glm-4.6`** and, among Flashes, only **`glm-5.3-flash` / `glm-5.3-flash-free`** — **`glm-4.6-flash` is not present**, so the `opencode/glm-4.6-flash` id resolves to no currently-documented artifact/spec.
- **The one peer study that ran it dropped it for lack of signal.** **arXiv 2606.13870 ("Mirage Probes," Jun 2026)** is the only academic source naming **"GLM-4.6-flash"** as a *callable endpoint*, and it explicitly reports: **"GLM-4.6-flash produces too few non-mirage responses on three of four benchmarks to support stable probing, so we drop it from the main results."** — i.e., a real but *unmeasurable* artifact, contributing **zero** quality numbers.
- **The remaining mentions are low-trust.** A **crazyrouter SEO blog** calls GLM-4.6-Flash "a smaller, faster variant… about 5× cheaper but slightly less capable" yet publishes **no Flash benchmark** (its "GLM-4.6" table — MMLU 83.2 / HumanEval 81.7 / GSM8K 91.5 — is a **content-farm fabrication** that contradicts Z.ai's own 200K-context spec, so it is not relied on). The only weight artifact found is a **community GGUF repackage** (`sartajbhuvaji/GLM-4.6-Flash-text`), not a Z.ai-published checkpoint with its own card or evaluation.

## What we did establish (documented, not scored)

- **Intent of the entry:** a **free, low-cost, text-only "Flash" tier** associated with the GLM-4.6 generation, described in the corpus as **128K context**, **tool-calling**, **reasoning**, priced **$0/$0** on the Z.ai Flash tier (cheaper/smaller than the 200K flagship).
- **Naming collision to guard (do NOT cross-credit):** **GLM-4.6V-Flash** is the **9B vision-language** model (**scored separately** — corpus entry `glm-4.6v-flash`); **GLM-4.7-Flash** is the **30B-A3B text** model (**scored separately** — `glm-4.7-flash`); **GLM-4.5-Flash** is another free text tier. None of these has been shown to be "GLM-4.6-Flash," and none of their numbers may be transferred onto this name.
- **Flagship vs Flash:** GLM-4.6 **flagship** numbers (AIME 25 / GPQA / LCB v6 / HLE / SWE-bench Verified, 200K ctx) are **the flagship's**, not the unmapped Flash's; inheriting them is exactly the reattribution the rules forbid.

> **Consistency check:** this is the **variant-with-no-own-measurement** pattern — closest to **`ling-3.0-flash-sante`** (health fine-tune whose specs were 100% inherited from an already-scored base and whose only variant-specific numbers were vendor/SEO-echoed) and **`owl-alpha`** (a real name whose evidence belonged to a base already credited). Like those, **no dimension scores are assigned**; unlike a thin-but-real artifact (e.g. `omen-alpha`, scored on one snapshot + hands-on), here there is **not even one benchmark tied specifically to GLM-4.6-Flash**, and its status as a distinct Z.ai text checkpoint is unconfirmed.

