- Method: public internet research (**Z.ai official `docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-4.6`** — flagship only: **200K ctx / 128K max output, text in/out**, "8 authoritative benchmarks… AIME/GPQA/LCB v6/HLE/SWE-bench Verified," no "Flash" text card → those are flagship numbers; **secondtalent.com GLM lineup (Sep 2026)** — free *text* Flashes = **GLM-4.7-Flash (30B/3B)** & **GLM-4.5-Flash**; **GLM-4.6V-Flash** = 9B **vision**; GLM-4.6 flagship (Sep 30 2025) shipped with no text-Flash sibling; **Artificial Analysis `glm-4-6-flash` → 404** (no Index/Speed/Cost); **OpenRouter `z-ai/glm-4.6-flash` → 404** (only GLM-4.6 flagship routed); **OpenCode Zen live table** — lists `glm-4.6`, `glm-5.3-flash`, `glm-5.3-flash-free`, **not `glm-4.6-flash`**; **arXiv 2606.13870 "Mirage Probes"** — "GLM-4.6-flash produces too few non-mirage responses… we drop it from the main results" (ran the endpoint, no usable quality data); **crazyrouter SEO blog** — "smaller, faster, ~5× cheaper," but **no Flash benchmark** and a fabricated flagship table (rejected); **HF `sartajbhuvaji/GLM-4.6-Flash-text`** — community GGUF repackage, not an official card. **Curated `meta`** — "no published Flash-specific benchmarks; Z.ai publishes flagship numbers only.")
- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** Z.ai publishes a **dated "GLM-4.6-Flash" text model card with its own evaluation**, **or** Artificial Analysis / OpenRouter / a tracker adds a **route and independent benchmark set attributed specifically to GLM-4.6-Flash** (not the flagship, not the 4.5/4.7-Flash siblings, not the 4.6V-Flash VLM). **Guards applied:** (1) do **NOT** import any **GLM-4.6 flagship** benchmark (AIME/GPQA/LCB/HLE/SWE-bench, 200K) onto this unmapped name; (2) do **NOT** cross-credit **`glm-4.7-flash` (30B-A3B)** or **`glm-4.6v-flash` (9B VLM)** numbers — those are separate scored artifacts; (3) reject the **crazyrouter** content-farm table as fabricated; (4) an arXiv run that **dropped** the endpoint is not a measurement. **No dimension scores are assigned.**
